  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: High temperatures throughout Northern \nNevada this afternoon will be around five degrees above normal \nfor this time of year. This will result in a moderate risk of \nheat-related illnesses. \n\nAn anticyclone aloft will move southeastward into the South\nCentral United States this afternoon. This will pull monsoonal\nmoisture northward into most of Northern and Central Nevada,\nresulting in isolated to scattered thunderstorms this afternoon\ninto this evening. The primary thunderstorm hazards will be \nlocalized flooding, small hail, wind gusts near 50 mph, and \ndangerous cloud to ground lightning strikes. \n\nMonsoonal moisture will remain in place over most of Northern and\nCentral Nevada Tuesday and Wednesday. Elko may break its all time\nrecord for precipitable water Tuesday afternoon. There is a \nslight risk of excessive rainfall in parts of Eastern Nevada \nTuesday. In addition, there is a Flash Flood Watch in effect for \nmost of Northern and Central Nevada Tuesday. Here are thunderstorm\nprobabilities for select locations in Eastern Nevada on Tuesday, \nJuly 21st, 2026:\n\nLund - 57% \nEly - 56%\nGreat Basin National Park - 53%\nEureka - 51%\nCurrie - 49%\nRuby Lake - 46%\nAustin - 41%\nTonopah - 41%\nWells - 38%\nElko - 33%\n\nScattered thunderstorms are expected throughout Northern and\nCentral Nevada Wednesday afternoon into Wednesday evening due to\nlingering monsoonal moisture. This monsoonal moisture will shift\neastward Thursday through Saturday, but thunderstorm chances\n(slight) will remain in the service area forecast. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding a moderate risk of heat-related illnesses in Northern\nNevada this afternoon. High forecast confidence in historically\nhigh atmospheric moisture content Tuesday. High forecast\nconfidence regarding a Flash Flood Watch for most of Northern and \nCentral Nevada Tuesday. High forecast confidence in a few strong \nthunderstorms in most of Northern and Central Nevada each\nafternoon and evening today through at least Wednesday. No\ndeviations from the NBM model output.",
